    "description": "Hemingray Glass Company\nNo. 45 Glass Insulator\nPressed Glass, Clear, Vintage\nA classic piece of American industrial history, this Hemingray No. 45 glass insulator was a standard component for telegraph and telephone lines during the 20th century. These insulators are sought after by collectors for their sculptural form and historical significance in the expansion of communication infrastructure. The No. 45 model features a robust double-petticoat design intended for high-performance electrical isolation.\nDouble petticoat construction for electrical insulation integrity\nClear glass with a subtle light aqua tint characteristic of period glass production\nEmbossed \"HEMINGRAY - 45\" marking prominently on the lower base skirt\nApproximately 3.75 inch base diameter and 4 inch total height\nCondition:\nExcellent vintage condition with no major chips or structural cracks. Inner and outer petticoats are intact. Original gloss is well-preserved with minor surface scratches consistent with age and utility service. Threaded core is clean and undamaged.",
